computation_methods:
The Gini coefficient is equal to the ratio of the sum of the total number of individuals and one to the difference between the total number of individuals and one, minus twice the sum of the products of each individual’s rank and weight, divided by the product of the mean welfare measure, the total number of individuals and the difference between the total number of individuals and one.

Formula:

G = (N + 1) / (N − 1) − 2 × Σ(rᵢ × wᵢ) / [μ × N × (N − 1)]

where:

G is the Gini coefficient;

N is the total number of individuals;

rᵢ is the rank of each individual, from the richest (1) to the poorest (N);

wᵢ is the weight of each individual;

μ is the mean welfare measure; and

Σ denotes summation across all individuals.
